{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_mqtt", "label": "MQTT", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_mqttactor", "label": "MqttActor", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "An abstract base you extend rather than a concrete class you drive with tell: declare subscriptions in the constructor, handle inbound traffic in onMessage, publish with this.publish. onReceive is sealed \u2014 the base dispatches to the hooks. It keeps its own richer subscription registry (per-topic QoS, several targets per pattern, deathwatch on each) because it predates the base class's desired-subscription mechanism.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_mqttoptionstype", "label": "MqttOptionsType", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_mqttcodec", "label": "MQTT codec", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The codec turns entities into bytes and back; the default is mqttJsonCodec(). A string or Uint8Array payload is sent RAW, any other value is encoded \u2014 so publishing a bare string as a JSON entity needs an explicit codec().encode call.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_mqttpayload", "label": "Lazily-decoding MqttPayload", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Decoding happens only when text() or entity() is called. A malformed payload throws MqttDecodeError inside onMessage, which the base catches and routes to onInvalidMessage (log + drop by default, no restart).", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_qos_levels", "label": "MQTT QoS levels", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "QoS 0 at-most-once, 1 at-least-once (the typical IoT balance), 2 exactly-once with a full handshake and rarely needed.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_retained_messages", "label": "Retained messages", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A retained message is stored by the broker and delivered immediately to any new subscriber \u2014 right for configuration and last-known-state, wrong for normal pub/sub where it keeps every old message visible forever.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_external_control", "label": "External control via MqttCommand", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A subscribe with no target delivers to the actor's own onMessage; with a target it fans out. An unsubscribe with no target removes all FOREIGN targets but leaves the subclass's constructor-declared subscription intact, so an external controller cannot silence it. Fan-out targets are deathwatched and a broker UNSUBSCRIBE fires once a pattern has no consumers left.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_persistent_session", "label": "Persistent session needs a stable clientId", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The broker tracks subscriptions and queued messages per-clientId, so a random clientId on each connect makes cleanSession:false useless.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_mqtt", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_mqttactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_mqtt", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_mqttoptionstype", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_mqtt", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_mqttcodec", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_mqtt", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_mqttpayload", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_mqtt", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_qos_levels", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_mqtt", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_retained_messages", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_mqtt", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_mqtt_external_control", "relation": "reference